# Monorepo environment guide — this root file is not loaded by either app.
# Copy the per-app examples for local development:
#   apps/web/.env.example   -> apps/web/.env.local
#   apps/agent/.env.example -> apps/agent/.env.local
# For hosted deployments, configure each app's variables on its own service.
# See those examples for the actual variables and optional features.
#
# Local host processes:
#   web: LANGGRAPH_API_URL=http://localhost:2024
#   agent: langgraphjs dev manages its development persistence.
#
# Local Docker Compose:
#   web: LANGGRAPH_API_URL=http://agent:2024 is injected automatically.
#   agent: DATABASE_URL for the Compose Postgres is injected automatically.
#   Compose environment entries override values in each app's .env.local.
#
# Hosted web + LangGraph Cloud agent:
#   web: set LANGGRAPH_API_URL and LANGGRAPH_API_KEY for the cloud agent.
#   agent: omit DATABASE_URL; platform persistence is managed by Agent Server.
#   web Supabase variables still configure separate business data.
#
# A self-hosted production Agent Server needs deployment-level persistence
# configuration. The application's DATABASE_URL is not a substitute for it.
